# BMW 3 Series E21 two-door saloon, 1975-1983.
#
# The first 3-series: a two-door saloon only, replacing the 02 range. Modelled
# with the six-cylinder front, twin round headlamps each side of a paired kidney
# grille, which the reference car at bmw-e21-4.jpg shows; the four-cylinder
# cars of the same shell carried a single lamp each side.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_3_Series_(E21)
# https://www.bmwe21.net/?page_id=106
#
# Dimensions 4.355 x 1.610 x 1.380 m, wheelbase 2.563 m, from the English
# Wikipedia dimension box, which repeats the BMW Group Archive figures and gives
# the 4,355 mm length as the European one (the North American car is 4,508 mm on
# its 5 mph bumpers). Body width is modelled at 1.571 m over the shell with the
# bumpers carrying the full 4.355 m length; the difference is 39 mm, less than a
# twentieth of a pixel at pak scale.
#
# Colours from the E21 paint register (BMWE21.net, "Paintwork & upholstery
# colors", which reproduces the 1978/79 and 1980-on brochure pages):
#   Polaris metallic  060, offered 1975-1984
#   Fjord metallic    037, offered 1975-1979
#   Schwarz           086, offered 1975-1982
#   Hennarot          052, offered 1980-1984
# Hennarot therefore starts in September 1980, with the model update, and the
# other three at launch. Weights silver 3, blue 3, black 2, red 2, total 10:
# no colour-split production statistics exist for the E21 (the register states
# this explicitly), so the split follows the length of each colour's offer and
# the general 1970s preference for silver and blue on imported executive cars.
# Provisional pending the central rebase, as the recent tranche is.
#
# Speed 180 km/h: the 320i's published top speed, the volume six-cylinder UK
# model; the 323i reached 190-200 km/h, and the four-cylinder cars 154-173 km/h.
# Comfort 105/488, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 105. Classes 1,2, matching the E36.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: June 1975 intro, retires staggered
# 1994-1998 on an eighteen- to twenty-one-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e21.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-e21.dae (53 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e21/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the compound
# curves of the bonnet and the shoulder are angular approximations, and the
# wheel centres read slightly further apart than the reference photograph's
# apparent wheelbase, which measures 0.63 of the length against the published
# 0.589. The published dimensions were kept.

obj=citycar
name=BMW3E21(PolarisSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1975
intro_month=6
retire_year=1995
retire_month=6
speed=180
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=105
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=488

